And you can retitle the same day.

“I lost my patience at bedtime.”
“I went back in and made it right.”

Both can be true. Tell yourself only the first and you can start to hear I’m a dad who loses his patience. Include the second and there’s something you can actually do again tomorrow. Over time, the story has more scenes to draw from because it changed what you did next.

That’s montage turned inward. What you tell yourself is the edit. What you do next gives you new footage.